  "title": "Cheugugi rain gauge and rainfall network",
  "summary": "In 1441, under King Sejong, Korea set up a state rain-monitoring network built around the cheugugi, a cylindrical copper gauge. The Annals of the Joseon Dynasty record a 3 September 1441 order that local magistrates measure rainfall regularly and report it to the central government. Korea.net dates the invention to 1442.",
